Z||000003||Tigger||11-27-2000||02:53 PM||||***Stimpy's Favorite Blues Playing***<P>Tigger: "Very Nice!"<BR>Stimpy: "WHAT?"<BR>Tigger: "I SAID IT LOOKS VERY NICE!"<BR>Stimpy: "WHAT?"<BR>Tigger: "IT SOUNDS GREAT!"<BR>Stimpy: "?"<BR>Tigger: *Gives a thumbs up*<BR>Stimpy: "Ohh, Right... Thanks!"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||stimpy||11-27-2000||03:25 PM||||Gee, thanks for the kudos, guys.  Hey sqoach, it's as easy as cheese to build one of these. The most time consuming part of the process is letting the fiberglass cure. The materials cost about $30 including the grill, terminal cup, and carpeting (cut from behind the seat of a pick-n-pull Fiero). The speaker was spendy ($180) and unfortunately due to the small size of the enclosure, you'll pretty much have to buy a speaker on par with that as far as quality goes.  Maybe Oreif or seanh can give some recommendations for other speakers, but I think the Polk is absolutely bulletproof.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||11-27-2000||06:12 PM||||He's right; it is easy to make.  Unless you have no fiberglass experience, like me.  It took the bulk of the time laying all the cloth out.  Real messy too.  Looks good, stimpy!  Can't wait until I get enough money to actually buy a sub.  All I can fit in there is an 8".  I made mine a little smaller.  Mine measures exactly 10" high, so I have to get an 8.  I might get some carpet from a Fiero at the salvage yard this weekend.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||11-27-2000||08:58 PM||||Ive never been a big fan of the aftermarket sub install, but I gotta hand it to ya Stimpmeister, that really looks good!<BR>Hmmm....now ya got me thinkin'!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||Seanh||11-27-2000||09:12 PM||||I would highly reccomend Polk Audio, on anything except computer speakers. I swear by Polk audio, I use Momo, but Dx and Db are both very good lines of speakers. If your looking for about the best you can get for a competition install, I would say Image Dynamics, Boston Acustics, MB Quarts, Polk Audio, maybe Alpines.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||11-28-2000||12:12 AM||||Hey seanh, what about a good speaker for this type of application that's more of a beer budget speaker? All those brands you listed are great for competition (I guess, I don't really follow all dat) but howzavout for the more modestly financed like our young friend fropuff?  Any really good 10" woofs for less then $100?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Seanh||11-28-2000||12:49 AM||||Actually, Polk Audio's EX models are good ones. Kickers are also along those lines. For a smaller budget, I would still say to stick with Polk Audio. EX is a fairly affordable line if I remember correctly. I think they go for about $80 for a 10" ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||11-28-2000||02:03 AM||||if you catch a sale you might be able to get a jl 10w1 or 10w0 for about $100.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||11-28-2000||01:15 PM||||JL is a good one to. I know of a place here to get Kickers for around $70 each, there pretty good speakers. Rockfords are a little bit more then those, but they are still pretty reasonable priced speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||11-28-2000||01:53 PM||||I bought a RockFord Fostgate XLC 8" for $60. A 10" should be no more than $80. Bass is great for the price. The non XLC is cheaper and bass is still great. I stongly recommend those if you are on budget.||||reg||1
Z||000013||vietnow||11-28-2000||02:10 PM||||rockfords are good, they are on sale around here also..<P>the local best buy has pioneer subs for buy one get one free like 60 for 8's and 70 10's and 80 for 12's<P><BR>on ampage, in my current car, i have a california amp. very nice, only 250 watt but good enough for me<BR>bought used at pawn shop for 100 bucks<P><P>------------------<BR>Vietnow --||||reg||1
Z||000014||stimpy||11-28-2000||02:37 PM||||But how will these lower priced speakers hold up in a small enclosure?  Get the extended warranty?  I dunno, just askin... ||||reg||1
